# Owned surface

Before planning or changing product scope, follow `AGENTS.md`, the reading map in
`docs/README.md`, and the sole implementation order in
`docs/technical/core-mvp-execution-plan.md`. Resolve product and safety
semantics through the authority order in those documents.

Cairn is a single-owner, self-hosted content, description, discovery, export,
and recovery platform with one configured repository and one SQLite catalog.
Its admitted first-party client experiences share that trusted kernel. Keep
work inside the current convergence lock and explicitly admitted client or
processor profiles. Treat deferred capabilities and non-goals according to the
authoritative requirements; an older plan, prototype, adapter, or acceptance
record does not re-admit them.

Do not copy retired capability lists or former product boundaries into this
rule. Do not start new MCP/CLI/AI integrations, runtime third-party code, a
kernel ABI or plugin store, or other deferred surfaces without a direct owner
request and the required contract review. Report conflicts instead of
broadening scope.
